# NOTE: node_modules is intentionally NOT excluded. This extension is not
# bundled (main = ./out/extension.js, plain tsc output), so it require()s its
# runtime dependency `vscode-languageclient` from node_modules at activation.
# Excluding node_modules stripped the dependency from the .vsix and crashed the
# extension on activation ("Cannot find module 'vscode-languageclient'"). vsce
# includes only the production dependency tree here, not devDependencies.
# If this extension ever adds a bundler (esbuild/webpack), re-add the exclusion.
# NOTE: bin/ is intentionally NOT excluded either. The release workflow copies the
# platform's natural-lsp server binary into bin/ before `vsce package --target`, and
# the extension launches <extensionPath>/bin/natural-lsp[.exe] at activation
# (feature 37). Excluding bin/ would drop the bundled server. (Guarded by
# src/test/unit/packaging.test.ts.)
.github/**
*.vsix
